    "result_text": "Tests are green.\n\n## What I changed\n\nI agree with the finding \u2014 it's the same duplication the codebase already solved for households, so I followed that precedent.\n\n- **Extracted `CheckOwnerCityCapacity.countInCity(OwnerRepository, String)`** \u2014 a static \"single source of truth\" for counting owners in a city case-insensitively, documented the same way `CheckOwnerHouseholdUnique.sameHousehold` is (explicitly noting it's shared so the two callers \"can never drift\").\n- **`CheckOwnerCityCapacity.service`** now calls the helper for its 50-owner gate.\n- **`AssignOwnerCustomerCode.service`** now calls the same helper for its per-city sequence number (`countInCity(...) + 1`), replacing the duplicated stream. I also dropped the javadoc note that had been standing in for the shared code.\n\nBoth the capacity gate and the customer-code sequence now derive from one definition of \"owners in this city\", so a future change to that definition can't make them disagree. I chose the static-helper approach over a new `OwnerRepository` query method to keep the change minimal and avoid touching all three repository implementations \u2014 matching the existing `findAll().stream()` idiom used throughout the owner functions.\n\nFull suite passes, including the `coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity` acceptance test.",
